<%- include('../partials/header', { title: 'Integration Setup' }) %>

<div class="toolbar">
  <h1>Ecwid Integration Setup</h1>
  <a class="link" href="/admin">Back</a>
</div>

<div class="setup-steps">

  <!-- STEP 1 -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="step-num">Step 1</div>
    <h2>Deploy this app to a public URL</h2>
    <p class="muted">The app must be accessible on the internet so Ecwid can reach it. Recommended platforms:</p>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Railway</strong> — <a class="link" href="https://railway.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">railway.app</a> · Connect your GitHub repo, set env vars, deploy.</li>
      <li><strong>Render</strong> — <a class="link" href="https://render.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">render.com</a> · Free tier available, auto-deploys from GitHub.</li>
      <li><strong>Fly.io</strong> — <a class="link" href="https://fly.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fly.io</a> · Good for SQLite (use a persistent volume).</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted"><strong>Important:</strong> SQLite writes to disk. On ephemeral platforms (Render free tier), use a persistent disk or the DB will reset on restart. Railway and Fly volumes are persistent.</p>
    <div class="setup-block">
      <div class="label">Environment variables to set on your host</div>
      <pre class="code-block">PORT=3000
BASE_URL=https://your-app.your-host.com
ECWID_STORE_ID=YOUR_STORE_ID
ECWID_ACCESS_TOKEN=YOUR_ACCESS_TOKEN
ECWID_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_CLIENT_SECRET
SESSION_SECRET=RANDOM_STRING_CHANGE_THIS
NODE_ENV=production
ALLOW_NO_ECWID=true</pre>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Your current <code>BASE_URL</code> is: <strong><%= baseUrl %></strong></p>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 2 -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="step-num">Step 2</div>
    <h2>Register a Native App in Ecwid</h2>
    <ol class="muted setup-list">
      <li>Log in to your Ecwid store at <a class="link" href="https://my.ecwid.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">my.ecwid.com</a></li>
      <li>Go to <strong>Apps → My Apps → Develop Apps</strong></li>
      <li>Click <strong>Create new application</strong></li>
      <li>Fill in a name (e.g. "Gift Registry")</li>
      <li>Under <strong>Control Panel iframe URL</strong>, paste:
        <div class="copy-row">
          <code class="copy-val"><%= baseUrl %>/ecwid/iframe</code>
          <button class="btn secondary copy-btn" data-val="<%= baseUrl %>/ecwid/iframe">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>Save the app. Copy the <strong>Client ID</strong> and <strong>Client Secret</strong> into your <code>.env</code> / host env vars.</li>
      <li>To get an <strong>Access Token</strong> for product lookups, go to <strong>Apps → My Apps</strong>, find your app, and click <strong>Get token</strong>. Copy that into <code>ECWID_ACCESS_TOKEN</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">Once connected, opening the app from your Ecwid control panel will pass a signed payload to <code>/ecwid/iframe</code>, which decrypts it and redirects to the admin.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 3 -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="step-num">Step 3</div>
    <h2>Embed the registry widget on your storefront</h2>
    <p class="muted">Add a registry page to your Ecwid Instant Site or any HTML page:</p>
    <ol class="muted setup-list">
      <li>In Ecwid, go to <strong>Website → Edit Site</strong></li>
      <li>Add a new page (e.g. "Gift Registries")</li>
      <li>Add a <strong>Custom HTML</strong> block to that page</li>
      <li>Paste the following snippet:
        <div class="copy-row">
          <pre class="code-block copy-val" id="embed-snippet">&lt;link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= baseUrl %>/public/styles.css" /&gt;
&lt;div id="registry-app"
     data-registry-app="1"
     data-store-id="<%= storeId %>"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;script src="<%= baseUrl %>/widget/registry.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</pre>
          <button class="btn secondary copy-btn" data-target="embed-snippet">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">The widget renders the registry list with search, and individual registry pages with add-to-cart for online registries.</p>
    <div class="setup-block">
      <div class="label">Alternatively, for a full standalone page</div>
      <p class="muted">Link customers directly to: <code><%= baseUrl %>/registry</code></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 4 -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="step-num">Step 4</div>
    <h2>Configure the order webhook (online registries)</h2>
    <p class="muted">When a customer places an order that includes a registry item, Ecwid will notify this app so the purchase is automatically marked on the registry.</p>
    <ol class="muted setup-list">
      <li>In Ecwid, go to <strong>Apps → My Apps → your app → Webhooks</strong></li>
      <li>Add a webhook for the <strong>order.created</strong> event</li>
      <li>Set the URL to:
        <div class="copy-row">
          <code class="copy-val"><%= baseUrl %>/webhooks/ecwid/order-created</code>
          <button class="btn secondary copy-btn" data-val="<%= baseUrl %>/webhooks/ecwid/order-created">Copy</button>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>Save. Ecwid will sign each webhook with your <code>ECWID_CLIENT_SECRET</code> — the app verifies this automatically.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="muted">The webhook only records a purchase if the order's extra fields contain a <code>registry_id</code>. This is set automatically when a customer browses from the registry widget.</p>
  </div>

  <!-- STEP 5 -->
  <div class="card">
    <div class="step-num">Step 5</div>
    <h2>Staff workflow</h2>
    <p class="muted">Here's how the day-to-day use works:</p>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li><strong>Create a registry</strong> — use the admin panel (this page). Choose "In-store" for couples who registered in person, "Online" for couples who want web guests to ship gifts.</li>
      <li><strong>Add items</strong> — search by SKU in the admin. Items are pulled from your Ecwid product catalog.</li>
      <li><strong>Share the link</strong> — use the "Copy shareable link" button on any registry and send it to the couple or share it on their invitation.</li>
      <li><strong>Record in-store purchases</strong> — when a guest buys a gift in the store, use "Mark purchase (in-store)" on the registry detail page.</li>
      <li><strong>Online purchases</strong> — recorded automatically via the webhook when guests check out on your Ecwid store.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</div>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll('.copy-btn').forEach(btn => {
  btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    const target = btn.getAttribute('data-target');
    const val = btn.getAttribute('data-val');
    let text = val;
    if (target) {
      const el = document.getElementById(target);
      if (el) text = el.textContent;
    }
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text.trim()).then(() => {
      const orig = btn.textContent;
      btn.textContent = 'Copied!';
      setTimeout(() => { btn.textContent = orig; }, 2000);
    });
  });
});
</script>

